  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Same-Origin Policy Beyond fetch",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Same-Origin Policy Beyond fetch",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What an Origin Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Origin== = **scheme** + **host** + **port**; all three must match",
                "`http://a.com`, `https://a.com`, `https://a.com:8443` are {red:three} origins",
                "Cookies use ==host + path==, not origin: they ignore port and scheme"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. What SOP Covers",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Cross-origin",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Form post, `img`, `script`, `link`, simple GET",
                  "{green:Sent}"
                ],
                [
                  "Reading the response",
                  "{red:Blocked}"
                ],
                [
                  "iframe `contentWindow` DOM",
                  "{red:Blocked}"
                ],
                [
                  "`localStorage`, IndexedDB",
                  "Per origin"
                ],
                [
                  "Cross-origin image on canvas",
                  "Canvas **tainted**"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "SOP blocks ==reads==, not sends",
                "So **CSRF tokens** are still required"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Relaxing It",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Non-simple request",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Preflight OPTIONS",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Server sends ACAO",
                    "sub": "Access-Control-Allow-Origin",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "JS reads response",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==CORS== is a server opt-in to let JS read the response",
                "`document.domain` is deprecated: use `postMessage` or CORS",
                "Wildcard `*` {red:cannot} be combined with credentials"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mental model",
              "text": "**Embedding** (script, img, iframe) is allowed; **reading** is denied by default."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Iframes and the sandbox Attribute",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Iframes and the sandbox Attribute",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Bare sandbox locks everything",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`<iframe sandbox>` with no value applies ==every restriction==",
                "Frame gets a unique ==opaque origin==",
                "No scripts, forms, popups, top navigation or plugins"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Tokens re-enable one feature each",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`allow-scripts` `allow-forms` `allow-popups` `allow-modals`",
                "`allow-same-origin` `allow-top-navigation` `allow-downloads`",
                "Add tokens ==one by one==, only what the widget needs"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "html",
              "lines": [
                "<iframe sandbox=\"allow-scripts\"",
                " src=\"https://widget.example\"></iframe>"
              ],
              "note": "Runs JS, but opaque origin: no cookies or storage"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Safe vs useless",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Tokens",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "No `allow-same-origin`",
                  "{green:Frame stays isolated}"
                ],
                [
                  "`allow-scripts` + `allow-same-origin`, same-origin content",
                  "{red:Frame removes its own sandbox}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Never combine",
              "text": "On same-origin `srcdoc` or `src`, scripts plus same-origin make the sandbox ==useless==."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Embed hygiene",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`allow=\"camera; geolocation; fullscreen\"` sets Permissions Policy",
                "Add `referrerpolicy` to limit the Referer sent",
                "Add `loading=\"lazy\"` on embeds"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Clickjacking: X-Frame-Options vs frame-ancestors",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Clickjacking: X-Frame-Options vs frame-ancestors",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Attack",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Attacker frames your page in an ==invisible iframe== (`opacity:0`)",
                "A {red:decoy button} sits under it; the victim's click lands on **your UI**",
                "The click carries the victim's ==session cookies=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Two Defences",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "X-Frame-Options",
                "CSP frame-ancestors"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Values",
                  "`DENY`, `SAMEORIGIN`",
                  "`'none'`, `'self'`, origins, wildcards"
                ],
                [
                  "Allow partner",
                  "{red:No}: no multi-origin list",
                  "{green:Yes}: list origins"
                ],
                [
                  "Where",
                  "Header only",
                  "Header only (not `<meta>`)"
                ],
                [
                  "Status",
                  "`ALLOW-FROM` obsolete, ignored",
                  "{green:Modern replacement}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "http",
              "lines": [
                "Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self' https://partner.com",
                "X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN"
              ],
              "note": "send both"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Both present: browsers with CSP support ==ignore X-Frame-Options==",
                "Send both anyway for ==old-browser== coverage"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`frame-ancestors` in a `<meta>` tag is ==ignored==",
                "`frame-src` / `child-src` control what **you** embed, not who embeds you",
                "`SameSite=Lax/Strict` cookies reduce impact, but are not a fix"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "text": "Which wins when both headers exist? **frame-ancestors**. Can XFO allow two origins? **No**. Does `<meta>` work? **No**, header only."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "postMessage and Origin Checks",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "postMessage and Origin Checks",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Sending",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`win.postMessage(data, 'https://app.example')`",
                "2nd argument = ==targetOrigin==: delivered only if it matches",
                "`'*'` leaks data to whatever page is loaded in that window"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Receiving",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "e.origin",
                    "sub": "exact ===",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "e.source",
                    "sub": "expected window",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "e.data",
                    "sub": "shape and type",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "window.addEventListener('message', e => {",
                "  if (e.origin !== 'https://app.example') return;",
                "  if (e.source !== frame.contentWindow) return;",
                "  if (typeof e.data?.id !== 'string') return;",
                "  label.textContent = e.data.id;",
                "});"
              ],
              "note": "textContent, never innerHTML"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Field",
                "Trust it?"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`e.origin`",
                  "Set by the browser, can't be forged; sandboxed or `data:` frames send {red:'null'}"
                ],
                [
                  "`e.source`",
                  "Says which frame sent it; origin alone can't"
                ],
                [
                  "`e.data`",
                  "{red:Attacker-controlled}: never to `innerHTML`, `eval`, `location`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Compare ==exactly==, never `indexOf`, `includes`, `endsWith` or regex",
                "`https://evil-app.example` passes `endsWith('app.example')`",
                "`https://evil-app.example.com` passes `indexOf` and substring checks"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Origin-checked is not authenticated",
              "text": "An allowed origin only says ==where== the message came from. Still validate `e.data`, and never trust `'null'` or skip the check."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Content Security Policy Basics",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Content Security Policy Basics",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Policy and Directives",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "http",
              "lines": [
                "Content-Security-Policy:",
                "  default-src 'self';",
                "  script-src 'self' https://cdn.example;",
                "  img-src * data:;",
                "  object-src 'none'"
              ],
              "note": "response header: allowed sources per directive"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Directive",
                "Controls"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`default-src`",
                  "fallback for the rest"
                ],
                [
                  "`script-src` `style-src` `img-src`",
                  "scripts, styles, images"
                ],
                [
                  "`connect-src`",
                  "fetch, XHR, WebSocket"
                ],
                [
                  "`frame-src`",
                  "what you embed"
                ],
                [
                  "`frame-ancestors` `base-uri` `form-action`",
                  "no fallback"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Inline Code and Rollout",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Inline scripts and eval are ==blocked== by default",
                "Allow inline with a per-response nonce `'nonce-R4nd0m'` or hash `'sha256-...'`",
                "`'strict-dynamic'` trusts scripts loaded by a nonced script",
                "Avoid `'unsafe-inline'` and `'unsafe-eval'`: they defeat XSS protection"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Report-Only",
                    "sub": "report-to / report-uri",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Read violations",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Enforce",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Wildcard or whole-CDN allowlist: JSONP/Angular gadgets bypass it",
                "No `object-src` or `base-uri`: injection bypass",
                "Static, reused nonce: must be new every response",
                "`default-src` skips `frame-ancestors`, `base-uri`, `form-action`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Defence in depth",
              "text": "CSP backs up ==output encoding==; it never replaces it."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Browser Isolation Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Browser Isolation Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Origins and iframes",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Same origin = ==scheme + host + port== all match",
                "SOP blocks ==reads==, not sends; **CORS** opts in",
                "Keep ==CSRF tokens==: cross-origin sends still go out",
                "`sandbox=\"\"` locks everything; add tokens one by one",
                "{red:Never} `allow-scripts` + `allow-same-origin` on same-origin content"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Clickjacking and postMessage",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Header",
                "Value",
                "For"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`Content-Security-Policy`",
                  "`frame-ancestors 'none'` or `'self'`",
                  "modern"
                ],
                [
                  "`X-Frame-Options`",
                  "`DENY` or `SAMEORIGIN`",
                  "legacy"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Send with an exact `targetOrigin`, never `'*'`",
                "Receive with exact `e.origin ===`; check `e.source`",
                "`e.data` is ==untrusted input==: validate it"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "addEventListener('message', e => {",
                "  if (e.origin !== 'https://app.example') return;",
                "  if (e.source !== frame.contentWindow) return;",
                "  handle(e.data); // validate shape",
                "});"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. CSP starter",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "http",
              "lines": [
                "Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'nonce-…' 'strict-dynamic'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; frame-ancestors 'self'"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Roll out safely",
              "text": "Test with ==Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only== first, read violations, then enforce."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Page on https://a.com runs fetch('https://a.com:8443/x') with no CORS headers on the reply. Does the request go out, and can the JS read the reply?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "The port differs, so it is a different origin.",
                "A simple GET still **is sent**, but the browser blocks JS from reading the response."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Spot the bug: a same-origin widget is embedded with sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin\". Why is the sandbox pointless?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "The frame keeps the real origin, so its script can reach the parent and remove the sandbox attribute.",
                "Fix: drop `allow-same-origin` so the frame gets an opaque origin."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A handler checks `e.origin.endsWith('app.example')`. Who gets through, and what is the fix?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`https://evil-app.example` also ends with it.",
                "Use `e.origin === 'https://app.example'`, and still validate `e.data`."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
